  "question": {
    "text": "The number of solutions of the equation \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{x}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{x}}+2\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{x}}+3\\right)=0\\) is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CvUzp",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DFXpN",
      "text": "3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YL29P",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uUcpj",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}}}=\\alpha \\quad \\mathrm{x}>0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left\\{9 \\alpha^2-9 \\alpha+2\\right\\}\\left\\{2 \\alpha^2-7 \\alpha+3\\right\\}=0 \\\\\n& (3 \\alpha-2)(3 \\alpha-1)(\\alpha-3)(2 \\alpha-1)=0 \\\\\n& \\alpha=\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{2}{3}, 3 \\\\\n& x=9,4, \\frac{9}{4}, \\frac{1}{9}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nSo, no. of solutions $=4$",
    "image": null
  },
